\section{Schema Label Renaming Experiment}
\label{app:renaming}

To test whether reducing pairwise SCS through label renaming improves accuracy, we conducted a controlled intervention on FewRel 80-relation RE (count 8, Qwen3-32B). We identified 14 high-SCS relation pairs (covering 12 unique relation types, as two types each appear in multiple pairs; mean SCS = 0.87) and replaced one label in each pair with a semantically distinct paraphrase chosen to minimize embedding cosine similarity (all-MiniLM-L6-v2). Examples: \textit{participant of} $\to$ \textit{event involvement} (SCS: 0.97 $\to$ 0.72), \textit{follows} $\to$ \textit{prior entry} (0.90 $\to$ 0.69), \textit{part of} $\to$ \textit{integral segment of} (0.90 $\to$ 0.64). The renaming reduced mean pairwise SCS from 0.87 to 0.67 ($\Delta = -0.20$). We ran the same 50 BCS-controlled batches (25 low-BCS, 25 high-BCS; 96 samples each) under both original (control) and renamed (treatment) label sets.

\begin{table}[h!]
